  <ym-title|From mission to local chart price><label|from-mission-to-local-chart-price>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Unit: YM-000026, trace selected-scale producer.

    <item>Status: draft; mathematical/source review requested, no whole-proof
    approval.

    <item>Imported Lean revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.

    <item>Manuscript: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/trace-mission-price.tex>.

    <item>Scope: reconstructs the limit passage from the selected mission and
    the finite-volume mileage estimate to the fixed-test local table price.
    It does not prove the mission's funded finite-cover producer or the
    probe/localization receipts consumed by mileage.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Source correspondence><label|source-correspondence>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Mathematical
  step>>|<cell|<strong|Exact Lean declarations and
  paths>>|<cell|<strong|Correspondence/status>>>|<row|<cell|Mission
  data>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.Mission>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/PriceLimit.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|terms>
  says eventually in <verbatim|i> that <verbatim|t i> converges along the
  selected ultrafilter to <verbatim|x i>; <verbatim|finances> provides one
  fixed complexity <verbatim|m> and, eventually in <verbatim|i> and
  ultrafilter-almost every pair <verbatim|p=(N,s)>, a <verbatim|Probe C m j
  p.2 p.1 ... (C.S.a j^5 \<bullet\> t i p)>. Here <verbatim|j=V_i.k> and
  <verbatim|k_i=summit(j)=Stern(V,i)>. The manuscript writes these two
  clauses mathematically.>>|<row|<cell|Finite-volume
  price>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.mileage>,
  <verbatim|YM.TraceExtension.Terrace/Meteor.lean>>|<cell|For each fixed
  complexity and grade-four field, mileage gives eventually in <verbatim|i>,
  then in <verbatim|p>, the two-site estimate at distinct sites for every
  tested grade-four transfer, scale parameter
  <verbatim|1\<leq\>b\<leq\>tilt_cap>, interior labels, and probe. The target
  is <verbatim|Tau(A) i (-100)>; the estimate is uniform over those
  finite-volume choices once the fixed test and complexity are
  fixed.>>|<row|<cell|Numerical mileage assembly>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.mileage>,
  together with <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.concert>, <verbatim|.outside>,
  <verbatim|.pulpit>, and <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.slides>; paths
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/{Meteor,Traveller,HomePort}.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|mileage>
  chooses the probe approximation and insertion approximation, applies the
  two reflected-cell product bounds and the exact three-term bilinear
  decomposition. The exponents are <verbatim|\<minus\>200>,
  <verbatim|\<minus\>295>, <verbatim|\<minus\>195>, and
  <verbatim|\<minus\>500>, summed to <verbatim|4
  Tau(\<minus\>195)\<leq\>Tau(\<minus\>100)>. The explicit reorganization
  appears in <verbatim|trace-local-pairing.tex>; <verbatim|concert>,
  <verbatim|outside>, and the probe receipt remain substantive upstream
  producers.>>|<row|<cell|Limit from measurements to selected
  table>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.proxi>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/SkyEar.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|proxi>
  states convergence of the two-entry numeric measurement to the selected
  table pairing at the scaled insertion point, after projecting both limiting
  labels. The mission array converges to the raw marker <verbatim|x i>; the
  finite grade-four height approximants converge in raw label space to
  <verbatim|Y 4 i w>, whose projection is <verbatim|X.U i 4
  w>.>>|<row|<cell|Geometry of the insertion
  point>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.kamago>, <verbatim|.beaconV>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/SkyEar.lean>>|<cell|The
  nearest-point vector has first coordinate <verbatim|ceil(b_i)> and all
  other coordinates 1. The identity <verbatim|X.r i=a_i b_i> rewrites the
  physical point as the scale-<verbatim|a_i> pair with cover labels
  <verbatim|(nearPoint(b_i),0)>. The link-period/sparse receipts make these
  sites distinct.>>|<row|<cell|Actual source
  application>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.ear_price>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/PriceLimit.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|ear_price>
  obtains the fixed <verbatim|m> from <verbatim|Mission.finances>, invokes
  mileage at the frame level, chooses the selected finite height
  <verbatim|T0=(V i).R N s \<langle\>4,...\<rangle\>>, establishes its
  <verbatim|Tested> and interior hypotheses, then applies <verbatim|proxi>
  and closedness of the norm sublevel set. The manuscript proves this
  limit-transfer argument in conventional notation.>>|<row|<cell|Mission
  producer>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Slate.hullage>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Slate/Phantom.lean>; finite-cover estimate
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.crestship>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Ell.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|hullage>
  builds the origin-convergent array and mission. Its <verbatim|finances>
  field is obtained through the finite-cover/funding theorem
  <verbatim|crestship> (called at fixed parameter 48) together with selected
  state and travel receipts. The actual proof of <verbatim|crestship>'s
  funding and probe-producing obligations is not included here.>>>>>

  <section|Checks and reads><label|checks-and-reads>

  Inspected the exact definitions/proofs in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/{PriceLimit,Meteor,SkyEar,Traveller,HomePort,Ell}.lean>
  and <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Slate/Phantom.lean>, using
  <verbatim|sed -n> and <verbatim|rg -n> to follow declarations and immediate
  calls. No Lean files were edited. No Lean, TeX, or test build was run.
  Blueprint validation has not been run for this new evidence file.

